cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "contract-triangulation: the aspect-ratio obstruction, proved"
abstract: >
  A Lean 4 proof, against Mathlib, of the geometric obstruction behind
  interactor-triangulation's two mesh properties. A triangle's aspect ratio is at
  least its longest edge over its shortest, so a bound on the ratio is a lower
  bound on edge length; a boundary that forces two mesh vertices closer than that
  admits no triangulation meeting the bound. The result fixes the threshold the
  C++ library validates its input against, so the constant is derived rather than
  tuned. Part of the multiplayer-fabric hexagonal architecture.
authors:
